From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vccorlib140: the C++/CX runtime: module start-up, activation by name, Platform exceptions (7009)

Programs written in C++/CX import vccorlib140.dll. Wine had none, so HexChat's
toast plugin (hcnotifications-winrt.dll) failed with "Library vccorlib140.DLL
not found". This new dll provides Platform::Details::InitializeData and
UninitializeData, GetActivationFactoryByPCWSTR (RoGetActivationFactory by class
name), Exception::Message and HResult, and the __abi_WinRTraise*Exception
raisers. The raisers throw a C++ exception whose object is the exception
handle, caught by the decorated handle-type names of the class and its bases
(the specific class, COMException, Exception, Object). The catch's copy holds
a reference, and the thrown handle is released after the catch. Only the
64-bit decorated names are exported.
---
